schemify 1 shbench

var C 1n

corner C1
  lib /pdk/m1.scs tt
  lib /pdk/m2.scs tt
  temp -40
corner C2
  temp 85

output st "settle(v(out), 10m)"
output ymxa ymax(v(out))

test B1
  code B1
  vnone output
test N1
  code N1
  corner C1
  vnone output
test N2
  code N2
  vnone output
test PA
  code PA
  vnone output
test TH
  code TH
  output st ymxa
test TR
  code TR
  design ./rr
  vnone output

code B1 spectre
  | temp options temp=-40
  | stb stb start=1 stop=1G dec=10 probe=IPRB0
code N1 spice
  | .temp -40
  | .options reltol=1e-5 gmin=1e-14
  | .noise v(out) V0 dec 10 1 1g
code N2 spectre
  | temp options temp=-40
  | noise (out in) noise start=1 stop=5 lin=4
code PA spectre
  | temp options temp=-40
  | pss pss fund=1M harms=3
  | pac pac start=1k stop=100k dec=5
code TH spice
  | .temp -40
  | .tran 1e-9 1u
code TR spectre
  | temp options temp=-40
  | dc dc param=temp start=-40 stop=125 step=5

--- report
needs_review:code	tb	analysis dc has no SPICE form: kept in the spectre block
needs_review:code	tb	analysis noise has no SPICE form: kept in the spectre block
needs_review:code	tb	analysis pac has no SPICE form: kept in the spectre block
needs_review:code	tb	analysis pss has no SPICE form: kept in the spectre block
needs_review:code	tb	analysis stb has no SPICE form: kept in the spectre block
needs_review:code	tb	maestro test N1: simulator option maxnotes=7 has no ngspice form: kept in the setup XML only
needs_review:code	tb	maestro test N2: noise inType=voltage: only port is written
needs_review:code	tb	maestro test N2: noise inVsrc=/V0: not a parameter of Spectre's noise
needs_review:config	tb	maestro test B1 has no output: a Schemify run gives it every one
needs_review:config	tb	maestro test N1 has no output: a Schemify run gives it every one
needs_review:config	tb	maestro test N2 has no output: a Schemify run gives it every one
needs_review:config	tb	maestro test PA has no output: a Schemify run gives it every one
needs_review:config	tb	maestro test TH runs simulator hspiceD: a Schemify run uses its own; the test goes back to Maestro as spectre unless the setup XML restores it
needs_review:config	tb	maestro test TR has no output: a Schemify run gives it every one
needs_review:corner	tb	corner C1 model /pdk/m2.scs sections tt ss: a corner group; only tt comes back (Schemify has no corner group)
needs_review:corner	tb	corner C1 var temperature -40,125: a corner group; only its first point -40 comes back (Schemify has no corner group)
needs_review:output	tb	maestro test TH: output ymxa is evaluated over corners; Schemify evaluates every output per job
needs_review:spec	tb	maestro test TH: spec of ymxa: ("tol" "0.1" "10%") has no Schemify spec (only > < and range)
needs_review:sweep	tb	maestro test B1: temperature sweep -40,27,125: only its first point -40 comes back (Schemify has no temperature sweep)
needs_review:sweep	tb	maestro test N1: temperature sweep -40,27,125: only its first point -40 comes back (Schemify has no temperature sweep)
needs_review:sweep	tb	maestro test N2: temperature sweep -40,27,125: only its first point -40 comes back (Schemify has no temperature sweep)
needs_review:sweep	tb	maestro test PA: temperature sweep -40,27,125: only its first point -40 comes back (Schemify has no temperature sweep)
needs_review:sweep	tb	maestro test TH: temperature sweep -40,27,125: only its first point -40 comes back (Schemify has no temperature sweep)
needs_review:sweep	tb	maestro test TR: temperature sweep -40,27,125: only its first point -40 comes back (Schemify has no temperature sweep)
